course: dictionary
lesson: 11470
title: Adverts and persuasion
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An advertisement is a notice, picture, film or message that tries to persuade people. To persuade means to get someone to buy something, use a service or go to an event. You see adverts on TV, on buses, on posters and on the internet.
explain: Look at this: «The TV advertisement showed a dancing robot, and the whole class wanted the toy.» The advert used a funny robot to make people want the toy. Advertisers use catchy slogans, bright pictures and big claims to persuade you.
explain: An advertisement can also be a public notice. «Mum read the job advertisement in the paper and applied for the post» means a notice about a job. Informally, «Tom's messy room is not a good advertisement for tidiness» means his room is a bad example of tidiness.
fact: An advertisement is a notice, picture, film or message that tries to persuade people to buy something, use a service or go to an event.
fact: An advertisement can also be a public notice about a job or something for sale.
fact: «Place an advertisement» means put a notice somewhere so people can see it.
fact: Adverts often use catchy slogans, bright pictures and exaggeration, which means saying something is better than it really is.
fact: Online adverts may trick you into clicking or buying, so check with a grown-up before you buy anything.
exercise: «The TV advertisement made the new cereal look amazing.» What is an advertisement? | Toys for babies | A broken television | *A notice, picture, film or message that tries to persuade people | A type of cereal
exercise: «Mum read the job advertisement in the paper.» What does job advertisement mean? | A bank form | *A public notice about a job | A map of the town | A story about a dragon
exercise: Why do adverts use catchy slogans and bright pictures? | *To persuade you to buy or do something | To hide the price | To show the weather | To make the page heavy
test: «The shop will place an advertisement in the window for its sale.» What does place an advertisement mean? | Close the shop for good | Throw the window away | *Put a notice up so people can see it | Sell the shop to a bank
test: «A pop-up advertisement promised free money, but it was a trick.» Why should you be careful with online adverts? | They are always true | *They may trick you into clicking or buying | They never have pictures | They are only printed on paper
exam: «Tom's messy room is not a good advertisement for tidiness.» In this informal sentence, what does advertisement mean? | A cleaning tool | *A bad example of something | A bright, funny film | A notice on a bus
